{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>אספה.</b> Some say it is like אוסיף (I will add). The correct interpretation is like אכלה, from the root of האף תספה (will be consumed). And if it is from a different binyan, the meaning is that no shepherd remains, that you not bring them. And compare the [divine] thoughts to arrows that come suddenly, with no ability to guard against them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:01.282873165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}